#!/usr/bin/env bash
set +e
cat >/tmp/article.html <<'EOF'
<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Building a Multi-Platform Social Media Growth System</title></head><body><main style="max-width:920px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.82"><h1>Building a Multi-Platform Social Media Growth System</h1><p>Social media growth is easier to improve when the campaign is treated as a system rather than a collection of disconnected tactics. Content quality, audience research, publishing consistency, profile optimization, analytics, conversion planning, and promotion all need to support a defined outcome.</p><p>Businesses comparing external growth providers can include <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/">SMM Fans Faster</a> in a wider evaluation. Platform coverage, service descriptions, delivery expectations, support, refill policies, order limits, and campaign fit are all useful comparison criteria.</p><h2>Start with audience and content</h2><p>Good distribution cannot compensate for content that gives users no reason to stay. Educational posts, demonstrations, comparisons, customer stories, and direct-response content each serve different parts of the funnel. A repeatable content structure makes it easier to identify which topics and formats generate the strongest response.</p><h2>TikTok campaign planning</h2><p>TikTok gives marketers rapid feedback on creative decisions. Hooks, pacing, editing, topic selection, and video length can all influence performance. Teams researching additional support can review resources about <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-followers">TikTok followers</a> and <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-views">TikTok views, followers, and likes</a>. The useful comparison is between those visible metrics and retention, comments, saves, shares, and profile visits.</p><h2>Instagram campaign planning</h2><p>Instagram requires a broader mix of formats. Reels can support discovery, carousels can explain detailed topics, Stories can maintain contact with existing followers, and highlights can organize important information. Marketers can review this guide to an <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/instagram-followers-website">Instagram followers website</a> while tracking profile visits, saves, shares, website clicks, direct messages, and conversions.</p><h2>Scale agency operations</h2><p>When an agency manages many campaigns, repetitive operational work can become a bottleneck. Technical teams can review the public <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/api">SMM API documentation</a> and the <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/smm-api-integration">SMM API integration</a> page when evaluating automation. Automation should support careful campaign management rather than remove quality checks.</p><h2>Track the complete customer journey</h2><p>Reach and impressions show how many people encountered the content. Engagement measures whether they cared enough to interact. Profile visits and website clicks show movement toward consideration. Leads, purchases, bookings, and revenue show whether the campaign created business value. Reviewing the whole funnel gives marketers a much more useful picture than follower count alone.</p><p>A balanced long-term system connects discovery, engagement, profile conversion, and business outcomes. The strongest campaigns keep testing content and distribution while measuring what actually changes audience behavior.</p></main></body></html>
EOF
resp=$(curl -sS --max-time 30 -X POST 'https://ship.page/deploy' -H 'Content-Type: text/html' --data-binary @/tmp/article.html)
echo "SHIPPAGE2_RESPONSE=$resp"
url=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get("url", ""))' 2>/dev/null)
if [[ "$url" == https://*.shipped.page/* ]]; then
 code=$(curl -sS -L -o /tmp/live.html -w '%{http_code}' "$url")
 if [ "$code" = "200" ] && grep -q 'smmfansfaster.com' /tmp/live.html; then echo "RESULT_URL=$url"; else echo "VERIFY_FAILED=$code $url"; fi
fi
